  <diagram id="notes" name="Design notes and sources">
    <mxGraphModel page="1" pageWidth="1400" pageHeight="1500">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="note" value="&lt;h1&gt;Design notes and evidence&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Status:&lt;/b&gt; Proposed system landscape, 12 October 2026. This is not evidence of deployed S/4HANA connectivity. It expands the supplied FootPrints / Ariba diagram toward the requested SAP S/4HANA interaction.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2&gt;How to read the landscape&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Solid arrows show the proposed read and case-processing path. Double arrows indicate request and response. Orange dashed arrows show an optional future SAP write path. The grey dashed arrow represents SAP authorization configuration, not business data flow.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The AWS outer boundary is an application boundary, not a single VPC. Runtime, Gateway and Bedrock are managed services. Specify subnet, endpoint, routing and egress placement in the network design.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Gateway invokes scoped Lambda targets using AWS permissions. Lambda adapters or established middleware separately authenticate to SAP. Native Gateway Lambda targets do not require each Lambda to implement an MCP server.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The SAP access layer has alternatives: approved direct released S/4 APIs, or existing enterprise APIs / SAP Integration Suite. Do not assume middleware exists or deploy both routes without a need. For private S/4 endpoints, validate VPC routing, DNS, VPN / Direct Connect and firewalls. SAP SaaS endpoints may require controlled outbound HTTPS.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;OData / SOAP are candidate backend interfaces, not confirmed active APIs. RFC/BAPI or IDoc should be used behind a supported integration adapter only where the actual landscape requires them.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Human approval is persisted in the case store and enforced by an authenticated workflow service. The action executor verifies approval, payload, source version, scope and idempotency; the model cannot approve its own action. Resolve ambiguous write results before retries.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Persistence and telemetry arrows are intentionally abbreviated: intake, workflow, adapters, review and executors also persist their relevant audit state. CloudWatch traces do not replace business audit evidence. Human-review callbacks resume the durable workflow.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2&gt;Needs validation before implementation&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;S/4 edition/release, API activation and metadata; source-of-truth and cross-system IDs; payment/clearing/settlement semantics; SAP technical or communication identity; authentication grant or certificates; network topology; AWS region and service availability; ITAR/data admission before extraction/inference; source freshness; business tolerances; SAP write scope and approval authority.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The provided diagram confirms FootPrints intake, Ariba-facing tools, one AgentCore investigation agent and human-approved FootPrints updates. S/4HANA and SPVR integration are extensions. The original scope note excludes ITAR routing and leaves Ariba corrections outside Phase 1.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2&gt;Official sources&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/gateway.html&quot;&gt;AWS — AgentCore Gateway&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/gateway-outbound-auth.html&quot;&gt;AWS — Gateway outbound authorization and target types&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/networking-and-content-delivery/private-connectivity-patterns-for-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-gateway-targets/&quot;&gt;AWS — Gateway private connectivity patterns and Lambda targets&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/tutorial-human-approval.html&quot;&gt;AWS — Durable human-approval workflow&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/observability.html&quot;&gt;AWS — AgentCore Observability&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.sap.com/docs/SAP_S4HANA_CLOUD/bb9f1469daf04bd894ab2167f8132a1a/4bf51821d3434ce7975de25c6fd8643b.html&quot;&gt;SAP — Purchase order read example&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.sap.com/docs/SAP_S4HANA_CLOUD/0fa84c9d9c634132b7c4abb9ffdd8f06/54eaa306f7014d179cc540aab92faa92.html&quot;&gt;SAP — General Ledger Accounting APIs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.sap.com/docs/CLOUD_INTEGRATION/sap-cloud-integration/setting-up-outbound-http-connections&quot;&gt;SAP — Integration outbound HTTP connections&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=18;spacing=20;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="40" y="40" width="1300" height="1400" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
